patch -p1 -l -f $* < $0
exit $?

From 269cc29ef0a97dc4a26807fc48f39c754f57fb9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Friedrichsmeier <thomas.friedrichsmeier@gnupg.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:58:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Provide help:/-protocol fallback without require .kde.org
 domain

We build kleopatra with a customized organization domain, and this would
disable the standard KF6 fallback handling for help:/-urls (if
khelpcenter is not available, open the online documentation at
docs.kde.org in a browser). This patch removes that check, to reinstate
the fallback.

See T8455, T8508
---
 src/util/kurlhandler_p.cpp | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/util/kurlhandler_p.cpp b/src/util/kurlhandler_p.cpp
index b556b18..2eec348 100644
--- a/src/util/kurlhandler_p.cpp
+++ b/src/util/kurlhandler_p.cpp
@@ -62,13 +62,6 @@ void KUrlHandler::openHelp(const QUrl &url) const

 QUrl KUrlHandler::concatDocsUrl(const QUrl &url) const
 {
-    if (QCoreApplication::organizationDomain() != QLatin1String("kde.org")) {
-        return {};
-    }
-
-    // KHelpCenter is not available and it's a KDE application, open the docs at docs.kde.org
-    // with the default web browser on the system
-
     QString path = url.path();
     // KHelpClient::invokeHelp() passes the anchor as an "anchor" query item
     const QString fragment = url.hasFragment() ? url.fragment() : QUrlQuery(url).queryItemValue(QStringLiteral("anchor"));
--
